==Faroese==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|non|fo}} ''[[#Old Norse|ætla]]''. Landt 1800<ref>Jørgen Landt: ''Forsøg til en Beskrivelse over Færøerne''. Copenhagen 1800, reprinted 1965. (p. 249)</ref> mentions it as typical Faroese in contrast to Danish ''[[tænke]], [[slutte]]''.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|[ˈatla]|lang=fo}} (''also in [[Suðuroy]]'')

===Verb===
{{fo-verb|ætlaði|ætlað}}

# to [[plan]], to [[intend]]
# to [[think]]

====Conjugation====
{{fo-conj-30|ætl}}

====Related terms====
* [[ætlan]] (plan, intention)

